# Build context filter for docker/qa-brain.Dockerfile and docker/browser.Dockerfile.
# Both are built with `context: .` from the repository root (see docs/ci-cd.md section 2,
# the `docker-build` job), so this file decides what BuildKit uploads to the daemon.
#
# Rule of thumb: everything `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile && pnpm build` needs stays;
# everything else goes. Keeping the context small is not only about speed -- anything sent
# here can end up in an image layer, and `.env`, `.qa-brain/` and `deploy/secrets/` must
# never do that (docs/security-threat-model.md T6).

# --- dependencies and build output (re-created inside the image) -------------------------
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo
**/.turbo

# --- secrets and local runtime state -----------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deploy/.env
deploy/secrets
.qa-brain
**/.qa-brain

# --- test output and caches --------------------------------------------------------------
coverage
**/coverage
test-results
**/test-results
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
**/.vite
**/.vite-temp
**/.cache

# --- VCS, CI and editor metadata ---------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.changeset
.idea
.vscode
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# --- prose: never needed to compile ------------------------------------------------------
docs
research
spikes
*.md
**/*.md
# LICENSE has no extension so `*.md` does not catch it, but be explicit: the image carries
# its Apache-2.0 licence (the `org.opencontainers.image.licenses` label points at it).
!LICENSE

# --- deployment artefacts: mounted at runtime, never baked in ----------------------------
deploy

# NOT ignored on purpose -- the build breaks without these:
#   package.json, */*/package.json   workspace manifests read by pnpm
#   pnpm-lock.yaml                   `--frozen-lockfile` refuses to run without it
#   pnpm-workspace.yaml              defines packages/*, apps/*, examples/*
#   .npmrc                           engine-strict, auto-install-peers (must match the lockfile)
#   tsconfig.json, tsconfig.base.json, */*/tsconfig.json, */*/tsup.config.ts
#   packages/, apps/                 sources, plus packages/store/migrations (shipped at runtime)
#   docker/                          kept so the daemon can always read the Dockerfile path
